 null}]}], "default_framework": "vllm", "plans": [{"backends": {"providers": [{"capabilities": {"activation_dtypes": [], "phases": [], "shape_constraints": [], "signature": "allreduce_fused_rmsnorm", "unsupported_features": [], "weight_dtypes": []}, "fused_op": "allreduce_fused_rmsnorm", "kernel_impl": "torch_allreduce_fused_rmsnorm", "library": "torch", "min_sm": null, "pip": "torch>=2.5", "provisioning": "pip"}], "signature": "allreduce_fused_rmsnorm"}, "backends_note": "", "description": "AllReduce-fused residual RMSNorm — TP>1 variant of `fused_add_rmsnorm`.\n\nNaive subgraph (the 3-op chain after a row-parallel linear's\npartial_sum output at TP > 1):\n\n  allreduce: y = ring_all_reduce(x_partial)\n  add:       z = y + residual            # in-place into residual\n  rmsnorm:   out = rmsnorm(z, weight)\n\nvLLM ships ONE custom CUDA kernel for the whole chain\n(`flashinfer_allreduce_residual_rmsnorm`) and sglang ships the\nequivalent (`tensor_model_parallel_fused_allreduce_rmsnorm`,\ndelegating to FlashInfer or to its own AITER path on AMD). The\nfused kernel avoids the two intermediate HBM write/read pairs that\nvanilla allreduce → add → rmsnorm would incur.\n\nRelationship to `fused_add_rmsnorm`\n-----------------------------------\n`fused_add_rmsnorm` matches the 2-op `(add, rmsnorm)` chain that\nappears at TP=1 (no allreduce present). `allreduce_fused_rmsnorm`\nadds the upstream `all_reduce` node to the pattern, so it ONLY\nmatches at TP>1 (the comm node only exists after the\nparallelism-comm injection pass).\n\nThe matcher's specificity sort puts higher-arity patterns\nfirst; the 3-node `allreduce_fused_rmsnorm` consumes the chain\nbefore `fused_add_rmsnorm` (2 nodes) gets a chance. At TP=1 the\nall_reduce node doesn't exist, so the larger pattern can't\nmatch and `fused_add_rmsnorm` fires instead. The two plans\nspecialize on disjoint deployment configurations without binding-\nyaml ordering hacks.\n\nCost preservation: Cost.combine sums each matched value